{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:induced-orientation-characterization","title":"lem:induced-orientation-characterization","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":1647,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#lem:induced-orientation-characterization","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:induced-orientation]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:adapted-frame-ambient-basis]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:nonvanishing-top-form-orientation]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-value-one]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"lem:induced-orientation-characterization","line":2749,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[The Induced Orientation is Lee's]\n\\label{lem:induced-orientation-characterization}\n\n\\uses{def:induced-orientation, lem:adapted-frame-ambient-basis, lem:nonvanishing-top-form-orientation, prop:volume-form-value-one}\n\n\n\n\nFor a $g$-orthonormal basis $(E_i)$ of $T_xM$, it is positively oriented for the induced orientation iff $(N_x,dF_xE_1,\\ldots,dF_xE_n)$ is positively oriented in $\\widetilde M$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{def:induced-orientation,lem:nonvanishing-top-form-orientation,prop:volume-form-value-one}\n\\sketch The contracted form evaluates on $(E_i)$ as the ambient volume form on the adapted basis, which is $1$ or $-1$ according to its orientation. The positivity criterion of Lemma \\ref{lem:nonvanishing-top-form-orientation} gives the equivalence.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[The Induced Orientation is Lee&#x27;s] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a696e64756365642d6f7269656e746174696f6e2d636861726163746572697a6174696f6e\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ainduced-orientation\">↗ def:induced-orientation</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Aadapted-frame-ambient-basis\">↗ lem:adapted-frame-ambient-basis</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Anonvanishing-top-form-orientation\">↗ lem:nonvanishing-top-form-orientation</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Avolume-form-value-one\">↗ prop:volume-form-value-one</a> <p></p>For a <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g$\">$g$</span>-orthonormal basis <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(E_i)$\">$(E_i)$</span> of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$T_xM$\">$T_xM$</span>, it is positively oriented for the induced orientation iff <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(N_x,dF_xE_1,\\ldots ,dF_xE_n)$\">$(N_x,dF_xE_1,\\ldots ,dF_xE_n)$</span> is positively oriented in <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\widetilde M$\">$\\widetilde M$</span>.  <p></p><section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ainduced-orientation\">↗ def:induced-orientation</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Anonvanishing-top-form-orientation\">↗ lem:nonvanishing-top-form-orientation</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Avolume-form-value-one\">↗ prop:volume-form-value-one</a> \\sketch The contracted form evaluates on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(E_i)$\">$(E_i)$</span> as the ambient volume form on the adapted basis, which is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$1$\">$1$</span> or <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$-1$\">$-1$</span> according to its orientation. The positivity criterion of Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Anonvanishing-top-form-orientation\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:nonvanishing-top-form-orientation\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a6e6f6e76616e697368696e672d746f702d666f726d2d6f7269656e746174696f6e\">8</a> gives the equivalence. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:induced-orientation","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:top-form-eq-of-basis","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:induced-orientation","title":"def:induced-orientation","label":"def:induced-orientation"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:adapted-frame-ambient-basis","title":"lem:adapted-frame-ambient-basis","label":"lem:adapted-frame-ambient-basis"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:nonvanishing-top-form-orientation","title":"lem:nonvanishing-top-form-orientation","label":"lem:nonvanishing-top-form-orientation"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-value-one","title":"prop:volume-form-value-one","label":"prop:volume-form-value-one"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hypersurface-volume-form-induced","title":"prop:hypersurface-volume-form-induced","label":"prop:hypersurface-volume-form-induced"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hypersurface-orientable-of-normal","title":"prop:hypersurface-orientable-of-normal","label":"prop:hypersurface-orientable-of-normal"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hypersurface-volume-form","title":"prop:hypersurface-volume-form","label":"prop:hypersurface-volume-form"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:induced-orientation-characterization","title":"lem:induced-orientation-characterization","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[The Induced Orientation is Lee's]\n\\label{lem:induced-orientation-characterization}\n\n\\uses{def:induced-orientation, lem:adapted-frame-ambient-basis, lem:nonvanishing-top-form-orientation, prop:volume-form-value-one}\n\n\n\n\nFor a $g$-orthonormal basis $(E_i)$ of $T_xM$, it is positively oriented for the induced orientation iff $(N_x,dF_xE_1,\\ldots,dF_xE_n)$ is positively oriented in $\\widetilde M$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{def:induced-orientation,lem:nonvanishing-top-form-orientation,prop:volume-form-value-one}\n\\sketch The contracted form evaluates on $(E_i)$ as the ambient volume form on the adapted basis, which is $1$ or $-1$ according to its orientation. The positivity criterion of Lemma \\ref{lem:nonvanishing-top-form-orientation} gives the equivalence.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:induced-orientation","title":"def:induced-orientation","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:adapted-frame-ambient-basis","title":"lem:adapted-frame-ambient-b